The injection molding machine uses plastic resin and molds to complete injection molding. The machine is mainly divided into two parts:
The molding process carried out in the injection molding machine consists of six basic steps:
Injection-the molten plastic from the injection unit of the machine is knocked into the mold;
Pressure keeping-the molten plastic injected into the mold is under pressure to ensure that all areas of the part are filled with plastic;
Cooling-allow the hot plastic to cool into the final part shape while still in the mold;
Mold opening-the clamping device of the machine separates the mold and divides it into two halves;
Ejection-the finished product is ejected from the mold.
