When PVC tarpaulin is used, it should be avoided to scratch the cloth with sharp tools, which will lead to the decline of waterproof performance of the cloth.
After the use of PVC tarpaulin, it should be unfolded, dried and packaged for reuse.
When the PVC tarpaulins are stacked and stored, they should be protected from moisture and rodents. They should be dried regularly according to the local humidity and climate.
During the transportation of PVC tarpaulin, the force should be even as much as possible to prevent the outer package from being damaged and the insulation quilt from being torn by brute force.
PVC tarpaulin is generally not fireproof, so it should be kept away from the fire source when it is used, especially when it is stored.
When the PVC tarpaulin is unfolded, it is necessary to avoid damage to the insulation quilt caused by pulling on the ground.
Before the PVC tarpaulin is unfolded, the ground should be checked to remove sharp objects to prevent the cloth damage on the surface of the insulation quilt.
