Have you done a few wrong operation of hydraulic breaker?
When the hammer is in operation, the drill rod should form a 90° right angle with the ground before operation. Tilting is prohibited to avoid straining the cylinder or damaging the drill rod and piston.
When the hit object is large or hard, don’t hit it directly. Choose the edge part to break it, which will complete the job more efficiently.
The hydraulic breaker hits the object continuously within one minute. If it fails to break, replace the hitting point immediately, otherwise the drill rod and other accessories will be damaged
This operation will cause the drill rod to break, the outer casing and the cylinder body to wear out abnormally, and shorten the service life of the hydraulic breaker.
It is forbidden to “pecking” by lowering the boom, which will cause a huge impact load and cause damage due to overload.
Except the drill rod, the hydraulic breaker must not be immersed in water or mud except for the drill rod. If the piston and other related parts accumulate soil, the service life of the hydraulic breaker will be shortened.
When your hydraulic breaker has not been used for a long time, follow the steps below to store it:
Use a hammer to knock the piston back to the back position; add more grease to the front head of the piston;
Place it in a room with a suitable temperature, or place it on a sleeper and cover it with a tarp to prevent rain.
Normally, the hydraulic oil replacement cycle of an excavator is 2000 hours, and the manuals of many breakers suggest that the hydraulic oil should be replaced in 800-1000 hours. Why?
When hydraulic breaker continues to work, the oil temperature will rise, please check the oil viscosity at this time.
If the viscosity of the working oil is too high, it will cause unsmooth operation, irregular blows, cavitation in the working pump, and adhesion of large valves.
If the viscosity of the working oil is too thin, it will cause internal leakage and reduce work efficiency, and the oil seal and gasket will be damaged due to high temperature.
During the working period of hydraulic breaker, the working oil should be added before the bucket is working, because the oil with impurities will cause the hydraulic components, hydraulic breaker and the excavator to work out of adjustment and reduce the work efficiency.
