The piston and cylinder of the hydraulic breaker are always strained. Do you know these reasons?
(1) Influence of hydraulic oil temperature
Affected by the dead weight and the inertia of the piston during reciprocating motion, the hydraulic oil film may not be established, so that the piston may not be established.
(2) Influence of impurities in hydraulic oil
In the actual working process of the hydraulic breaker, the phenomenon of partial strike of the drill rod often occurs, which will generate lateral force and cause the piston to be pulled.
The general fault is to check whether the nitrogen valve of the upper cylinder is leaking, or to fill the upper cylinder with nitrogen, and use the excavator to put the upper cylinder of hydraulic rock breaker into the pool to have a look. Whether there is air leakage from air bubbles, if these steps cannot check the source of air leakage, then the nitrogen gas is likely to be leaking from the oil passage of excavator hydraulic breaker!
