The outer circulation double-layer curtain wall system is generally a glass curtain wall composed of single-layer glass or laminated glass and non-heat-insulating profiles, and the inner layer is a curtain wall composed of insulating glass and heat-insulating profiles. Both ends of the ventilation layer formed by the inner and outer curtain walls are equipped with air inlet and exhaust devices, and sunshading devices such as louvers can also be installed in the passage.
In summer, open the air intake and exhaust vents of the ventilation layer, and the air temperature of the ventilation layer rises naturally under the sunlight, forming a bottom-up air flow. Due to the “chimney effect”, the heat in the channel is taken away and reduced The temperature of the inner glass surface reduces cooling costs.
Thereby forming superior temperature conditions, achieving the purpose of delivering fresh air from the ventilation layer to the room, thereby optimizing the ventilation quality of the building. Adjustable shutters or curtains are set in the passage, which can effectively adjust the sun shading and create a more comfortable environment for the interior.
