Analysis of Causes and Control Measures of Condensation in Insulating Glass News
The dew point refers to the temperature at which the humidity of the air sealed in the air layer reaches a saturated state, and is an important indicator reflecting the sealing performance of the insulating glass. When the surface temperature of the glass in the hollow layer is lower than the dew point of the air in the air layer, the water in the air will condense or frost on the inner surface of the glass.
So can we determine the air dew point by air temperature and relative humidity?
Calculate the dew point temperature at a certain temperature and relative humidity by querying the partial pressure of saturated water vapor at different temperatures. See the table below for the partial pressure of saturated water vapor at different temperatures under standard atmospheric pressure.
So how to quickly determine the dew point of insulating glass in practice?
GB 50411-2019 “Building Energy-saving Engineering Construction Quality Acceptance Standards” “Appendix E Insulating Glass Sealing Performance Test Method” gives the insulating glass sealing performance test method, that is, the dew point test method.
The sealing performance of insulating glass in GB 50411-2019 is tested according to “Appendix E”, which is actually to test the dew point of insulating glass; while the sealing performance in GB/T 11944-2012 includes “water-gas seal durability” and “air-tight seal” “Durability” and “dew point” are in a parallel relationship. When GB 50411-2019 is undergoing engineering acceptance, the sealing performance of insulating glass is the dew point.
