Here is to briefly share with you the five elements that affect the quality of insulating glass!
The raw glass used to make insulating glass can be colorless float glass, coated glass, toughened glass, laminated glass, etc. Should avoid the use of ordinary flat glass, ordinary flat glass transparency and strength are not up to the requirements.
The cutting size of the glass shall be strictly implemented according to the requirements of the drawing. At the same time, the operator shall pay attention to the glass surface without any obvious defects such as scratches and bubbles.
Users should choose the appropriate molecular sieve according to their own needs and molecular sieve should have the appropriate particle size (1-1.5mm) and hardness. In addition, the environment of the use of molecular sieve should be dry, and the filling molecules should be used within 1.5 hours to ensure the quality of insulating glass.
