OLED screen can drive the organic film to emit light through current, which has the characteristics of self luminescence. Each pixel of OLED screen can emit light by itself without relying on additional backlight.
This pixel itself does not emit light and does not participate in image display, but it is made of transparent materials. Therefore, the transparent OLED screen not only takes into account the display of color images, but also obtains a certain transparent effect.
Therefore, most of the transparent LED screens we see are used in the window or large stage of the outer wall of the mall. It is difficult to see a small transparent LED screen.
In fact, some transparent screen products have appeared in our lives.
In 2011, Lenovo S800, the first color transparent screen mobile phone, came out. Compared with Xperia pureness, the transparency of S800 has been greatly improved.
At present, transparent screen technology is still developing. And the transparent screen that looks cool and full of sense of science and technology is also controversial.
On the other hand, a mature transparent device is not only transparent on the screen, but also needs to make the components such as battery, processor, camera, microphone and speaker transparent, which is still difficult at present. If complete transparency is achieved, the assembly, strength and surface wear resistance of mobile phones also need to be considered by manufacturers and users.
