This is mainly because the application of insulating glass can improve the heat insulation and sound insulation effect of doors and Windows, so that the doors and Windows products can not only shelter from wind and rain, but also have significant energy saving effect, reducing the cost of heating in winter and cooling in summer.
1, trough aluminum type insulating glass: this kind of insulating glass was introduced in the 1980s, relatively mature, but the processing technology is more complex.
Aluminum strip type insulating glass: this kind of insulating glass started late in China, but the manufacturing process is simple, so it has a wide application range and is promoted quickly.
According to the national inspection standards, how to arrange the production to meet the requirements of insulating glass? Since there are many similarities between the two kinds of insulating glass in the technological process, the common technological process of them is briefly analyzed.
Glass cutting can be done by hand or by machine, but should be guaranteed to meet the size requirements. In the process of operation, workers should pay attention to the glass surface should not have scratches, even quality, no air bubbles, slag and other obvious shortcomings.
After washing the glass should be assembled into insulating glass within 1 hour, in addition to ensure that there is no friction between the glass and the glass, there is a semi-finished glass storage car, separated between the glass pieces.
But it should be noted that the desiccant should choose a regular manufacturer of qualified products, in order to ensure the effective use of desiccant.
Use butyl glue as the first seal, play a role in blocking gas.
Practice has proved that the life of single channel sealing insulating glass is only about 5 years, while the life of double channel sealing insulating glass can be as long as 20 years or even more than 40 years. Therefore, the development of double channel sealing insulating glass is the general trend.
Aluminum strip insulating glass, the outer part of the aluminum frame and the edge of the glass should be 5-7mm apart after the sheet, for coating the second sealant, the two-component glue should be evenly coated along one side to prevent bubbles, and the residual on the glass surface should be scraped off after coating.
First of all, the design requirements of the stacking rack should take into account the characteristics of hollow glass, and the stacking rack should have a certain inclination. However, the bottom plane and side parts should always be kept 90 degrees, so as to ensure that the two bottom glass edges of the insulating glass can be placed vertically on the stacking rack.
In order to improve the effect of sound insulation and heat insulation of insulating glass, manufacturers take out the air inside the insulating glass and inject inert gas into the insulating glass. This process makes the performance of insulating glass further improved.
