Our planet Earth is a fairly complex system in which there are millions of interactions between living beings and the elements of nature. It is so complex and comprehensive that it is impossible to study planet Earth as a single whole.
The geosphere is made up of several layers. The surface layer of the Earth, which usually varies between 500 and 1.000 meters, which is made up of soil and sedimentary rocks.
The lower basalt layer in which the oceanic crust is found and has a thickness of about 10-20km.
It is composed of a gas mixture of nitrogen (78%), oxygen (21%), and other gases (1%). It is the area where clouds and precipitation form, and its importance is that makes it possible for our planet to be habitable.
As you can see, each subsystem of the Earth is composed of different elements and has a key function for life on the planet. But the one we are going to focus on in this article is the biosphere.
In the marine part, it also includes the areas of surface waters and the depths of the oceans where life exists. Outside the biosphere and the limits that we have more or less imposed, there is no terrestrial life.
We define system as that set of components that interact with each other, and also with external agents, in such a way that they act as a set that maintains a functionality in between. That is why the biosphere is perfectly defined as a system since they have a set of species that interact with each other, and in turn, interact with other elements that do not belong to the biosphere, but belong to the geosphere, atmosphere and hydrosphere.
Therefore, in the biosphere there are biotic factors that are represented by all those communities of living beings that interact with each other and with the rest of the Earth's subsystems. Those communities of living things are made up of producers, consumers, and decomposers.
In the biosphere, in general, living beings do not live in isolation, but rather need to interact with other living beings and with abiotic factors. That is why, in nature there are different levels of organization.
This level of organization occurs in nature when the organisms of a certain species of plants, animals or microorganisms associate in a common time and spaces. That is, various species of plants and animals cohabit in the same space and they use the same resources to survive and proliferate.
