It is the highest point of the wave. It is famous for surfers and is recognized by the white water and foam that is generated when the wave begins to bend and fall.
The period of a wave is the one that measures the time that occurs between one wave and another. This measurement is made by choosing a fixed point and calculating the time it takes for the crest of the wave to pass to the second crest.
Frequency is somewhat similar to period, but with the difference that it only measures the total number of waves that pass through a reference point per unit of time.
Amplitude is the distance between the still water line and the crest of the wave. You could say that it is the height of the middle of the wave.
