Micronesia is a region located in the Pacific Ocean and part of a continent made up mainly of islands and several archipelagos: Oceania. Micronesia consists of hundreds of small islands scattered throughout the western Pacific Ocean and is politically divided into 8 territories.
Micronesia is one of the three main cultural regions in this part of the Pacific Ocean, the other two being Melanesia and Polynesia. Some history
Along with Palau, the Micronesian states form the Caroline Islands, located about 800 kilometers east of the Philippines. Consisting of 607 islands spread over an area of 2500 square kilometers, the effective area of the state is 700 square kilometers, of which more than half corresponds to the island of Pohnpei.
Legislative power is in the hands of Congress, a unicameral system with 14 members: 4 senators for 4-year terms and 10 members representing their districts for 2-year terms.
The highest body of the judiciary is the Supreme Court of the Federated States of Micronesia, whose members are elected by the President with the approval of 2/3 of Congress. Judges have life sentences.
