Heautoscopy is a term used in psychiatry and neurology for the hallucination of “seeing one’s own body at a distance.” The disorder is closely related to Autoscopy. It can occur as a symptom in schizophrenia and epilepsy, and is considered a possible explanation for doppelganger phenomena.
