Sailors sailed to the purported location of Hy-Brasil in large numbers, curious about what they could discover there. According to records, John Jay Jr. set out from Bristol, England, in 1480, and spent two weeks at sea before returning with his dreams dashed.
The crew met an older guy who promised them gold and silver, according to the captain’s story. The enormous black bunnies and the mystery magician encountered there were the icing on the cake that astonished the sailors.
Although the narrative was undoubtedly difficult to comprehend even for those living at the time, there was a second trip headed by Alexander Johnson that took place around the same time and confirmed Nisbet’s testimony.
Hy-Brasil appears in several stories and on various maps, therefore it’s probable that there’s some truth to this narrative somewhere. Some think the isle is the abode of Irish gods, while others believe it is inhabited by a sophisticated society.
What’s more, the top and bottom of the text began with the coordinates of Hy-Brasil, or at least the location widely referred to by mariners throughout the years. The deciphered message also included an inexplicable origin year of 8100.
In this scenario, it’s probable that Hy-Brasil was a memory of an actual mythological land that withstood the test of time via people who vividly remembered of it, one generation after another.
In any event, the mystery of this mythical island will pique the interest of people who want to learn more about our ancient history, because it might be a reminder of an alternative historical version of the world we live in.
The “Yonaguni Monument” or also known as the “Yonaguni Submarine Ruins” is a prehistoric submerged rock formation that is formed in weird large clusters up to 5 floors high and it is highly believed to be a ‘completely man-made’ artificial structure.
The most attractive and strange feature is a rectangularly shaped formation measuring about 150 by 40 metres and about 27 metres tall and the top is about 5 metres below the sea level. This is the largest structure that looks like a complicated, monolithic, stepped pyramid.
Two closely spaced pillars which rise to within 2.4 metres of the surface
A triangular depression with two large holes at its edge
On the other hand, some of those who have studied the formation, such as geologist Robert Schoch from the Boston University, Oceanic Geoscience Professor Patrick D. Nunn from the University of the South Pacific, suggest that it is either a completely natural formation or it was a natural rock structure that was later possibly used and modified by humans in the past.
Actually, the Yonaguni Monument reminds us of another mysterious and more sensational undersea structure, The Baltic Sea Anomaly, which is believed to be a wreck of ancient alien-ship. You could read the story of this strange undersea mega-structure here.
