Chromosome abnormality or chromosome disorder is a missing, extra, or irregular portion of chromosomal DNA. People with chromosome disorders suffer from various diseases and disabilities –one common disorder is Down’s Syndrome which is a genetic chromosome 21 disorder causing developmental and intellectual delays.
Inside the nucleus of our each body cell are microscopic bodies called chromosomes that are responsible for the function and reproduction of each cell in our body, empowering us to live. Chromosomes are made of two large molecules or strands of deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA), actually, these strands are called the genes, that give the instructions that control over the cell’s function and reproduction.
