Manual derusting: This is a relatively simple derusting method, which uses scraper, hammer, steel brush, abrasive cloth (paper), grinding wheel and other tools to knock, shovel, grind and scrape the rust. Its advantages are simple and easy to operate, low cost, widely used in rust removal of equipment and facilities in use, but the disadvantages are high labor intensity, low efficiency, unstable quality and poor working environment.
High pressure water derusting: the impact of high-pressure water flow (plus the grinding effect of abrasive) and water prying action are used to destroy the adhesion of rust and coating to steel plate, which is characterized by no dust pollution, no damage to steel plate and good effect. However, the steel plate after rust removal is easy to return to rust, so it is necessary to apply special wet derusting coating.
