2 Sayings month of June and their meaning
June is a month in which both minimum and maximum temperatures they start to rise considerably, especially in the center and in the Mediterranean region of the country, where the values are already between 20 and 30º (or more in some parts of the south of the Iberian Peninsula). In the rest, the mercury in the thermometer stays around 15 and 25ºC.
Sayings month of June and their meaning
Early June water, great evils remedies: The rains at the beginning of the month are very beneficial, as they will help the crops grow and bear fruit correctly.
Capricious June, or drought, or flood: this month can be either very dry or very humid, there is no middle ground.
Sunny and bright June, puts you in a good mood: As the days get longer, people's mood improves, as we can enjoy almost 15 hours of light.
Waters in June neither fruits nor grasses in July: The problem with the rains this month is that they can spoil the crops.
June 21 is as long as none: the 21st is the longest day of the year, it is the Summer Solstice.
For San Julieta, the rain more than give takes away: Santa is on the 16th, and at that time many horticultural plants are about to mature. If it rains, they can be spoiled.
