We must not confuse dark matter with antimatter. The latter is a form of ordinary matter, like the matter that constitutes us, but it is composed of elementary particles with opposite electrical signs: positive / negative.
Dark energy is a form of energy that exists throughout the universe and tends to accelerate its expansion by repelling gravity or force. It is estimated that 68% of the energetic matter in the universe belongs to this type, and it is a very uniform form of energy that does not interact with any other fundamental force in the universe, which is why it is called "dark".
