Due to barriers to humid air: large mountainous barriers prevent the arrival of rain clouds, so that when the air rises, the rain falls and the air loses moisture, forming a warm desert in windward areas (that is, places where the wind blows). As examples we have the Cuyo desert in Argentina, or the Judea desert in Israel.
