We are going to analyze part by part the different layers of the ionosphere to see in detail their composition and importance. Region D
This name has been given in honor of the American engineer Arthur E. Kennelly and the English physicist Oliver Heaviside. This layer extends more or less from 90 km, where layer D ends up to 160 km.
